  ⚠ vue(valid-v-model): 'v-model' directives aren't supported on <div> elements.
   ╭─[valid_v_model.tsx:1:16]
 1 │ <template><div v-model="foo"></div></template>
   ·                ─────────────
   ╰────
  help: Use `v-model` only on form elements (`input`/`select`/`textarea`) or components.

  ⚠ vue(valid-v-model): 'v-model' directives require no argument.
   ╭─[valid_v_model.tsx:1:26]
 1 │ <template><input v-model:aaa="foo"></template>
   ·                          ───
   ╰────
  help: Remove the argument; native elements don't support `v-model:foo`.

  ⚠ vue(valid-v-model): 'v-model' directives don't support the modifier 'aaa'.
   ╭─[valid_v_model.tsx:1:26]
 1 │ <template><input v-model.aaa="foo"></template>
   ·                          ───
   ╰────
  help: Native elements only support `.lazy`, `.number`, and `.trim`.

  ⚠ vue(valid-v-model): 'v-model' directives require that attribute value.
   ╭─[valid_v_model.tsx:1:18]
 1 │ <template><input v-model></template>
   ·                  ───────
   ╰────
  help: Give `v-model` a binding target, e.g. `v-model="value"`.

  ⚠ vue(valid-v-model): 'v-model' directives require the attribute value which is valid as LHS.
   ╭─[valid_v_model.tsx:1:27]
 1 │ <template><input v-model="a + b"></template>
   ·                           ─────
   ╰────
  help: Use an identifier or member expression, e.g. `foo` or `foo.bar`.

  ⚠ vue(valid-v-model): 'v-model' directives don't support 'file' input type.
   ╭─[valid_v_model.tsx:1:30]
 1 │ <template><input type="file" v-model="b"></template>
   ·                              ───────────
   ╰────
  help: File inputs can't be programmatically set; use a `ref` and a `change` listener instead.

  ⚠ vue(valid-v-model): 'v-model' directives cannot update the iteration variable 'x' itself.
